Q8. Calculate the Area and Circumference of a Circle
Question:
Write a program to calculate the area and circumference of a circle using its radius.

Sample Input:
Radius = 7


Expected Output:
Area = 153.94
Circumference = 43.98


Formula:
- Area = π × Radius × Radius
- Circumference = 2 × π × Radius
Python Code:
import mathradius = 7area = math.pi * radius ** 2circumference = 2 * math.pi * radiusprint("Area =", round(area, 2))print("Circumference =", round(circumference, 2))



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    const float PI = 3.14159265;
    float radius = 7;

    float area = PI * radius * radius;
    float circumference = 2 * PI * radius;

    printf("Area = %.2f\n", area);
    printf("Circumference = %.2f\n", circumference);

    return 0;
}


Java Code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        final double PI = Math.PI;
        double radius = 7;

        double area = PI * radius * radius;
        double circumference = 2 * PI * radius;

        System.out.printf("Area = %.2f%n", area);
        System.out.printf("Circumference = %.2f%n", circumference);
    }
}



Q9. Calculate Total Marks and Percentage
Question:
Write a program to calculate the total marks, average marks, and percentage of a student in five subjects. Each subject carries a maximum of 100 marks.

Sample Input:
English = 85
Mathematics = 90
Science = 78
Computer = 95
Hindi = 82


Expected Output:
Total Marks = 430
Average Marks = 86.00
Percentage = 86.00%


Formula:
- Total = Sum of all subject marks
- Average = Total / Number of Subjects
- Percentage = (Total / Maximum Marks) × 100
Python Code:
english = 85mathematics = 90science = 78computer = 95hindi = 82total = english + mathematics + science + computer + hindiaverage = total / 5percentage = (total / 500) * 100print("Total Marks =", total)print("Average Marks =", round(average, 2))print("Percentage =", round(percentage, 2), "%")



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    int english = 85;
    int mathematics = 90;
    int science = 78;
    int computer = 95;
    int hindi = 82;

    int total = english + mathematics + science + computer + hindi;

    float average = total / 5.0;
    float percentage = (total / 500.0) * 100;

    printf("Total Marks = %d\n", total);
    printf("Average Marks = %.2f\n", average);
    printf("Percentage = %.2f%%\n", percentage);

    return 0;
}


Java Code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int english = 85;
        int mathematics = 90;
        int science = 78;
        int computer = 95;
        int hindi = 82;

        int total = english + mathematics + science + computer + hindi;

        double average = total / 5.0;
        double percentage = (total / 500.0) * 100;

        System.out.println("Total Marks = " + total);
        System.out.printf("Average Marks = %.2f%n", average);
        System.out.printf("Percentage = %.2f%%%n", percentage);
    }
}



Q10. Calculate the Total Salary of an Employee
Question:
Write a program to calculate the gross salary of an employee using basic salary, house rent allowance (HRA), and dearness allowance (DA).

HRA is 20% of the basic salary, and DA is 10% of the basic salary.

Sample Input:
Basic Salary = 30000


Expected Output:
Basic Salary = 30000.00
HRA = 6000.00
DA = 3000.00
Gross Salary = 39000.00


Formula:
- HRA = Basic Salary × 20 / 100
- DA = Basic Salary × 10 / 100
- Gross Salary = Basic Salary + HRA + DA
Python Code:
basic_salary = 30000hra = basic_salary * 20 / 100da = basic_salary * 10 / 100gross_salary = basic_salary + hra + daprint("Basic Salary =", basic_salary)print("HRA =", hra)print("DA =", da)print("Gross Salary =", gross_salary)



C Code:
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    float basic_salary = 30000;

    float hra = basic_salary * 20 / 100;
    float da = basic_salary * 10 / 100;

    float gross_salary = basic_salary + hra + da;

    printf("Basic Salary = %.2f\n", basic_salary);
    printf("HRA = %.2f\n", hra);
    printf("DA = %.2f\n", da);
    printf("Gross Salary = %.2f\n", gross_salary);

    return 0;
}


Java Code:
public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double basicSalary = 30000;

        double hra = basicSalary * 20 / 100;
        double da = basicSalary * 10 / 100;

        double grossSalary = basicSalary + hra + da;

        System.out.printf("Basic Salary = %.2f%n", basicSalary);
        System.out.printf("HRA = %.2f%n", hra);
        System.out.printf("DA = %.2f%n", da);
        System.out.printf("Gross Salary = %.2f%n", grossSalary);
    }
}


